<div class="marketing-page" data-controller="scroll-reveal">
<%= render 'shared/marketing_header' %>

<!-- Header -->
<section class="mkt-hero" style="padding: 4rem 0 5rem;">
  <div class="mkt-inner">
    <span class="mkt-hero__eyebrow" style="margin-bottom: 1.25rem; display: inline-flex;">
      <span class="mkt-hero__eyebrow-dot"></span>
      Last updated: <%= Date.current.strftime("%B %d, %Y") %>
    </span>
    <h1 class="mkt-hero__title" style="font-size: clamp(2rem, 4.5vw, 3.25rem);">Privacy Policy</h1>
    <p class="mkt-hero__subtitle" style="max-width: 36rem;">
      We collect the minimum needed to run the service. We don’t sell your data
      and we don’t run analytics on you.
    </p>
  </div>
</section>

<!-- Content -->
<div class="mkt-section bg-white">
  <div class="mkt-inner--narrow">

    <div class="mkt-highlight-box mkt-highlight-box--blue mkt-reveal" data-scroll-reveal-target="item" style="margin-bottom: 3rem;">
      <strong>The short version:</strong> We collect only what we need to run your account.
      We don't track you, sell your data, or use it for advertising. During the trial, your data
      lives on our servers. After you purchase, the PWA still talks to us today. On Omarchy,
      local mode never sends tasks to us.
    </div>

    <div class="mkt-prose mkt-reveal" data-scroll-reveal-target="item">

      <h2>How we think about your data</h2>
      <p>
        Your lists belong to you. We try to collect as little as we can, say so plainly,
        and give you export and delete in Settings.
      </p>

      <h2>1. Information We Collect</h2>

      <h3>1.1 Account Information</h3>
      <ul>
        <li><strong>Email address</strong> - used for account identification and communication</li>
        <li><strong>Name</strong> - optional display name for personalisation</li>
        <li><strong>Password</strong> - securely hashed and stored (we cannot see your actual password)</li>
      </ul>

      <h3>1.2 Trial Information</h3>
      <ul>
        <li><strong>Trial start date</strong> - when your 7-day trial began</li>
        <li><strong>Trial expiration date</strong> - when your trial ends</li>
        <li><strong>Download status</strong> - whether you've downloaded the app to your device</li>
      </ul>

      <h3>1.4 Omarchy (Linux desktop)</h3>
      <p>
        On <a href="https://omarchy.org/">Omarchy</a> you can use Peponi without an account.
        Tasks then live only on that machine and are never sent to peponi.to.
        If you sign in with a paid account, we copy your existing tasks onto the machine once;
        new work stays there. Trial accounts cannot use that paid sign-in.
      </p>

      <div class="mkt-highlight-box mkt-highlight-box--green">
        <strong>What we don't collect:</strong> We do NOT collect analytics, tracking data, or behavioural information.
        We don't use cookies for tracking. We don't sell your data to third parties. Ever.
      </div>

      <h2>2. How We Use Your Information</h2>

      <h3>2.1 Essential Services</h3>
      <ul>
        <li>Provide access to your account and data</li>
        <li>Manage your 7-day free trial</li>
        <li>Enable app download after purchase</li>
        <li>Send essential account notifications (password changes, trial reminders)</li>
      </ul>

      <h3>2.2 Data Processing</h3>
      <p>
        Your data is processed only on our secure servers and is never shared with third parties
        except as required for payment processing (Polar) and email delivery (Brevo).
        These services are bound by their own privacy policies and data protection agreements.
      </p>

      <h2>3. Your Data Rights (GDPR Compliance)</h2>

      <h3>3.1 Right to Access</h3>
      <p>
        You can export all your data at any time through the app's export feature.
        This includes all your pages, tasks, and account information in a machine-readable JSON format.
      </p>

      <h3>3.2 Right to Rectification</h3>
      <p>
        You can update your account information at any time through the settings page -
        including your name, email address, and password.
      </p>

      <h3>3.3 Right to Erasure</h3>
      <p>
        You can delete your account and all associated data at any time through the settings page.
        This action is irreversible and will permanently remove all your data from our servers.
      </p>

      <h3>3.4 Right to Data Portability</h3>
      <p>
        After purchasing the app, you can download it to your device and have complete control over your data.
        You can also export your data in standard JSON format at any time.
      </p>

      <h3>3.5 Right to Object</h3>
      <p>
        You can opt out of non-essential communications at any time.
        We only ever send essential account-related emails.
      </p>

      <h2>4. Data Security</h2>

      <h3>4.1 Technical Safeguards</h3>
      <ul>
        <li>All data is encrypted in transit using HTTPS/TLS</li>
        <li>Passwords are hashed using bcrypt (industry standard)</li>
        <li>Database access is restricted and monitored</li>
        <li>Regular security updates and patches applied</li>
      </ul>

      <h3>4.2 Data Minimisation</h3>
      <p>
        We only collect the minimum data necessary to provide our service.
        We don't collect analytics, tracking pixels, or behavioural data.
        We don't use third-party analytics services.
      </p>

      <h2>5. Data Retention</h2>

      <h3>5.1 Active Accounts</h3>
      <p>
        During the 7-day trial we keep your pages and tasks on our servers so you can use the website.
        After purchase, the PWA still talks to our servers today. On Omarchy, local mode never
        sends tasks to us, and paid sign-in is a one-time copy onto your machine, not ongoing hosting.
      </p>

      <h3>5.2 Trial Accounts</h3>
      <p>
        If your trial expires and you don't purchase the app, we will retain your data for 7 days
        to allow you to complete your purchase. After 7 days, your data will be permanently deleted.
      </p>

      <h3>5.3 Deleted Accounts</h3>
      <p>
        When you delete your account, all your data is permanently removed from our servers within 7 days.
        This includes all pages, tasks, and account information.
      </p>

      <h2>6. Third-Party Services</h2>

      <h3>6.1 Payment Processing</h3>
      <p>
        We use Polar for payment processing. Polar (as Merchant of Record) handles your payment information according to their privacy policy.
        We do not store your payment details.
      </p>

      <h3>6.2 Email Delivery</h3>
      <p>
        We use Brevo for email delivery. Brevo processes your email address for delivery purposes only
        and is bound by their privacy policy.
      </p>

      <h2>7. Children's Privacy</h2>
      <p>
        Our service is not intended for children under 13. We do not knowingly collect personal information
        from children under 13. If you are a parent or guardian and believe your child has provided us with
        personal information, please contact us.
      </p>

      <h2>8. Changes to This Policy</h2>
      <p>
        We may update this privacy policy from time to time. We will notify you of any material changes
        by email or through the app. If you keep using the service after that, you accept the new policy.
      </p>

      <h2>9. Contact Us</h2>
      <p>
        If you have any questions about this privacy policy or your data rights, please contact us:
      </p>
      <div style="background: #F0EDEA; border: 1px solid #D8D4CC; border-radius: 0.5rem; padding: 1.25rem 1.5rem;">
        <p style="margin: 0; color: #4E5C64;">
          <strong>Email:</strong> <a href="mailto:support@peponi.to">support@peponi.to</a><br>
          <strong>Subject:</strong> Privacy Policy Inquiry
        </p>
      </div>

      <div class="mkt-highlight-box mkt-highlight-box--green" style="margin-top: 2.5rem;">
        <strong>Your privacy matters:</strong> This policy is designed to be transparent and easy to understand.
        If anything is unclear, email us. We’ll explain.
      </div>

    </div>
  </div>
</div>

<%= render 'shared/footer' %>
</div>
